{{!-- A2, "three-column grid", on an author archive: the profile as a rail beside a card grid.

	{{> "author/a2"}}

The crumb sits above the grid here rather than inside the profile, because the profile is a
column and a breadcrumb belongs to the page. It is a span, not a link, for the reason
author/header.hbs records: Ghost has no Authors Directory URL to point it at.

`grid-cols-[280px_minmax(0,1fr)]` and not a bare `1fr` for the second track: bare `1fr` means
`minmax(auto,1fr)`, whose floor is the column's min-content width, so a long headline in a card
would push the grid wider than the page instead of wrapping.

The grid's track is 280px against the tag archive's 330 — the cards sit in the narrower column
left over beside the rail, and the design tightens the gutters to match.

THE PAGINATION IS INSIDE THE COLUMN, which is why this partial draws it and author.hbs draws it
only for the List layout. Called at page level it centres on the page and lands under the rail,
100px left of the cards it pages through; `bare=true` takes the `container` off the control so it
centres inside the track instead. `{{pagination}}` reads `page`/`pages`/`prev`/`next` off the
context, and a partial called with no hash arguments keeps its caller's — this Surface's own
pagination, the same object author.hbs would have passed. --}}
<div class="container pt-14">
	<nav
		aria-label="{{t "Breadcrumb"}}"
		class="text-muted mb-8 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">
		<span>&larr; {{t "All writers"}}</span>
	</nav>

	<div
		class="max-stack:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] max-stack:gap-10 grid grid-cols-[280px_minmax(0,1fr)] items-start gap-18">
		{{#with author}}
			{{> "author/rail" total=../pagination.total}}
		{{/with}}

		<section
			id="posts"
			aria-label="{{t "Posts"}}">
			<div class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(280px,100%),1fr))] gap-x-8 gap-y-11">
				{{#foreach posts}}
					{{> "archive/card" tagEyebrow=true eyebrowSpacing="mt-4" titleClass="text-[22px]" excerptSpacing="mt-2.5"}}
				{{else}}
					<p class="font-body text-muted">{{t "No posts by this writer yet."}}</p>
				{{/foreach}}
			</div>

			{{pagination bare=true pt="pt-13"}}
		</section>
	</div>
</div>
